  "chapter": {
    "number": 122,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(123) A Song of Degrees."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "To you who dwell in heaven have I lifted up my eyes.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Behold, as the eyes of servants are directed to the hands of their masters, and as the eyes of a maidservant to the hands of her mistress; so our eyes are directed to the Lord our God, until he have mercy upon us.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Have pity upon us, O Lord, have pity upon us: for we are exceedingly filled with contempt.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Yes, our soul has been exceedingly filled with it:",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 230
          },
          {
            "text": "let the reproach be to them that are at ease, and contempt to the proud.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 230,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Or, we are the reproach of them that are at ease.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 122,
          "verse": 4
        }
      }
    ]
  },
